              "start": 10
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Souter asked: \u201cAt what point in the litigation did you first raise the Government speech argument?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 20,
              "start": 20
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Souter, justice Souter followed up: \u201cWhy isn\u2019t that a First Amendment violation?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 28,
              "start": 28
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked whether the government may discriminate based on content, framing it as a First Amendment question."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 38,
              "start": 38
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Souter asked: \u201cSo this case \u2014 your claim would disappear if this town in Utah had passed an ordinance saying we adopt the Ten Commandments Monument?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 42,
              "start": 42
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked: \u201cIs there a historical basis for that, or you just made it up?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 48,
              "start": 48
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Alito asked: \u201cIsn\u2019t merely allowing the monument to be built on public property sufficient acceptance?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0003-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 56,
              "start": 56
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked: \u201cWould that be enough?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0003-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 61,
              "start": 61
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, justice Breyer requested documents: \u201cGive one and I\u2019ll read it. Give me three; I\u2019ll read them.\u201d"
      }
