              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioners, the case involves a dispute over a privately donated, permanent monument that Pleasant Grove City, Utah, wishes to place on public property."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioners",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Petitioners argue that the Tenth Circuit erred and that the First Amendment\u2019s Free Speech Clause forces Pleasant Grove City to accept and erect the monument."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "City of Pleasant Grove",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "cc18b9aac33c234b973dedf4d41831ac061fa7c88b31993932229295c27e88b1",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-cc18b9aac33c-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 40,
              "start": 40
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to City of Pleasant Grove, the city argues that the government's involvement is limited to the act of selecting the monument."
      }
    ],
